<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Native AOT keeps only what it can see being used. Neo4j.Driver 6.3.0 builds its table of server-error exceptions at
  run time: Neo4jExceptionFactory reflects over the exported Neo4jException types, reads their ErrorCode attribute and
  invokes each one's non-public (FailureMessage, Exception) constructor. Those constructors are never called directly,
  so trimming removed them; the factory then threw inside a type initializer, and every server-side error (wrong
  password, constraint, syntax, transaction timeout) surfaced as TypeInitializationException in the native build
  (gate test test_wrong_password_is_reported_as_authentication, 20 November 2026).

  Keeping the driver's public namespace whole keeps those types, attributes and constructors. It does not silence the
  analysis warnings (IL2026, IL2080 on Neo4jExceptionFactory); the gate's store-failure tests are the evidence.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Neo4j.Driver">
    <namespace fullname="Neo4j.Driver" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
